<title>UK: Tunstall makes profit warning.</title>
<headline>Tunstall makes profit warning.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Tunstall Group Plc said on Monday that overall group profit for the year ending September 30, 1997 is expected to be below that achieved in 1995-96.  </p>
<p>The alarm and emergency communication systems firm said that current economic difficulties in Germany and the strength of sterling are beginning to bite.</p>
<p>Tunstall said that German revenues were likely to be 20 percent lower and that current expectations for the year are for a loss in Germany roughly equivalent to last year's profit.</p>
<p>It said that profit expectations at its core UK telecoms business remain unchanged and noted that it intends to maintain a progressive dividend policy.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 4019</p>
